OL,3,GNEWSAScot carves out a place at world
OL,4,Awood-chopping championships
OL,5,
OL,6,FA Scot will fly the flag for his home
OL,7,Fcountry this weekend when he takes part
OL,8,Fin an international competition for
OL,9,Fextreme wood chopping.
OL,11,FGraham Turner, a fencing contractor
OL,12,Ffrom the Scottish Borders, will travel
OL,13,Fto Germany to take part in the
OL,14,FTimbersports world championships.
OL,16,FHe goes through an articulated lorry of
OL,17,Fwood every year while training alone -
OL,18,Fwith the results often going to his own
OL,19,Flog burner or those of his
OL,20,Flong-suffering neighbours.
OL,23,APub: 27-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
FL,428,420,260,160,0,100
